window.LINES={"hello": "Hello, scientist! Welcome to my Cell Museum. I'm your guide today!", "sneeze": "ACHOO!", "scattered": "Oops! That big sneeze blew my parts all over the museum.", "help": "Can you help me find them? We'll follow them, room by room.", "miccheck": "First, let's check I can hear you. Say: Hello, Celly!", "heardyou": "I heard you! You sound great.", "nohear": "I can't hear you right now. That's okay. You can tap instead.", "tapmode": "Today you can tap your answers.", "bigq": "Today's big question: how are plant and animal cells the same, and different?", "room1": "Room one has a time machine. We're going back to sixteen sixty-five. Hold on!", "hooke_hi": "This is Robert Hooke, a scientist. He made his own microscope.", "cork": "He's looking at a thin slice of cork. Cork comes from the bark of a tree.", "tapboxes": "Look through his microscope. Tap three of the little boxes.", "boxes_a": "Little boxes, everywhere! Hooke called them cells.", "rooms_q": "Why did Hooke call them cells?", "rooms_a": "Monks lived in small rooms called cells. The boxes looked just like those little rooms.", "scope_intro": "Microscopes got better and better. Tap the oldest one first.", "sc_hooke": "Hooke's microscope, in sixteen sixty-five. It magnified about thirty times.", "sc_1800": "The early eighteen hundreds. About two hundred times.", "sc_today": "Today's light microscopes. Up to one thousand five hundred times!", "sc_wrong": "Not that one yet. Which one is older?", "mummy": "In eighteen twenty-five, Dr Granville studied a mummy. Why did he see more than Hooke?", "mummy_joke": "Ha! Mummies don't wave. Try again.", "granville_a": "His microscope magnified more. Better microscopes show more detail.", "smaller": "As microscopes got better, scientists found smaller and smaller parts of cells.", "tb": "Granville said the mummy died of cancer. In two thousand and nine, scientists said it was TB, a lung disease.", "brick1": "Room two is the building blocks room. Here's one cell: tap to add more!", "brick_tissue": "Lots of the same cells, working together. That's a tissue!", "brick_you": "Cells and tissues build a whole living thing. Like you!", "block_q": "Which sentence is true?", "block_a": "Yes! A cell is the basic building block of all living things.", "tissue_q": "What is a tissue?", "tissue_a": "A group of the same type of cells, working together.", "hanky": "That's a paper hanky! Not that kind of tissue.", "room3": "Room three is the word workshop. Look! My parts are here!", "watch": "Remember this bit from the video? Let's watch.", "buildintro": "To get each part back, we build its name.", "w_nucleus": "This part is the control centre of the cell. Its name has three beats.", "w_cytoplasm": "This part is a watery jelly, where most activities happen. Three beats.", "w_membrane": "This part is a very thin bag that keeps the cell together. Two beats.", "w_mitochondria": "Tiny jelly-bean shapes, where respiration releases energy. Five beats.", "w_chloroplast": "Green discs that make food for a plant. Its name has three beats.", "w_vacuole": "A large storage space in a plant cell. Its name has three beats.", "tapbeats": "Tap the beats in the right order.", "notyet": "Not that one yet. Which beat comes next?", "built": "You built it!", "drum": "Now tap the drum once for each beat, and say the beats with me.", "sayword": "Now say the whole word.", "again": "Let's try once more, slowly. Listen.", "yousay": "Now you say it.", "goodtry": "Good try! We'll practise that one again another day.", "back_nucleus": "My nucleus is back! Now I can control things again.", "back_cytoplasm": "My cytoplasm is back! Lovely, watery jelly.", "back_membrane": "My membrane is back! It holds me together.", "back_mitochondria": "My mitochondria are back! I feel full of energy!", "fourback": "Four parts back! Nine Cats Make Music: nucleus, cytoplasm, membrane, mitochondria.", "chloro_means": "Chloro means green. Chloroplasts are green!", "notmine": "Wait, that's not mine! It's a plant part. Let's keep it safe for a friend.", "vac_means": "Vacu means empty, like a vacuum cleaner. It's a big space for storing.", "room4": "Room four is the animal cell room. Listen, then tap each part on me.", "ask_nucleus": "Tap the part that controls the cell.", "ask_cytoplasm": "Tap the watery jelly, where most activities happen.", "ask_membrane": "Tap the very thin bag around the outside.", "ask_mito": "Tap a part where respiration releases energy.", "is_nucleus": "That's the nucleus. It controls the cell.", "is_cytoplasm": "That's the cytoplasm, the watery jelly.", "is_membrane": "That's the cell surface membrane. It keeps me together, and controls what enters and leaves.", "is_mito": "Those are the mitochondria. Respiration releases energy there.", "whatname": "What is this part called? Say its name.", "sayit": "Say it with me.", "foundall": "You found every part! Nine Cats Make Music!", "mito_q": "Here's a tricky one. Mitochondria make energy. True or false?", "mito_a": "False! Mitochondria don't make energy. They release it from food, by respiration.", "room5": "Room five is the plant cell room. Look who's here!", "cab_hi": "It's my friend, Very Wobbly Cabbage! He's a plant cell.", "cab_parts": "Plant cells have my four parts, plus some extras.", "cab_how": "For each part, say: plant, or both. Or tap a box.", "q_plantboth": "Plant cells only, or both?", "yes_both": "Yes, both! Plant and animal cells have it.", "yes_wall": "Yes, plant cells only! The cell wall supports the plant cell.", "yes_chloro": "Yes, plant cells only! Chloroplasts make food for the plant.", "yes_vacuole": "Yes, plant cells only! The vacuole is a large storage space.", "no_plant": "Hmm, I don't have one of those. Try the other box.", "no_both": "Hmm, I've got one of those too! Try the other box.", "vwc": "Very Wobbly Cabbage: vacuole, wall, chloroplasts. The plant extras!", "cablabel": "Now let's label Cabbage's cell. Tap each part as I say it.", "pl_wall": "Tap the cell wall, the thick box around the outside.", "pl_wall_a": "The cell wall is a box with holes in it. It's made of cellulose, which is very strong.", "pl_mem": "Now tap the cell surface membrane. It's just inside the wall.", "pl_mem_a": "Wall outside, membrane inside. The membrane controls what enters and leaves.", "pl_vac": "Tap the vacuole, the big space in the middle.", "pl_vac_a": "The vacuole is a large storage space, filled with cell sap.", "pl_chl": "Tap a chloroplast, a little green disc.", "pl_chl_a": "Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll. They make food for the plant, by photosynthesis.", "pl_nuc": "Tap the nucleus.", "pl_cyto": "Tap the cytoplasm, the watery jelly.", "pl_mito": "Tap one of the mitochondria, the little jelly beans.", "tap_wrong": "Not that part. Look again.", "sevenlabels": "All seven parts labelled! That's a plant cell.", "photo_intro": "Here are leaf cells, magnified two hundred and seventy-five times. Spot a green disc, and tap it!", "photo_mito_q": "Now look closely. Can you see any mitochondria?", "photo_mito_a": "No! They're too small to see here. You can see the chloroplasts, but not the mitochondria.", "bb_start": "Brain break! Stand up and copy me.", "bb_fist": "Make a fist. That's the nucleus, the boss!", "bb_wiggle": "Wiggle your fingers. That's the jelly cytoplasm.", "bb_circle": "Draw a big circle around you. That's the membrane.", "bb_box": "Now make a big box with your arms. That's the cell wall!", "bb_energy": "Pump your arms and shout: energy! That's the mitochondria.", "bb_heard": "I heard you! What a lot of energy!", "bb_moves": "Great moves!", "bb_breath": "Now sit down, and take one slow breath.", "room6": "Room six is full of mystery cells. Plant or animal? Say it, or tap a box.", "det_wrong": "Hmm, look for clues. Try the other box.", "d_cheek": "A cheek cell. No cell wall, so it's an animal cell!", "d_leaf": "A leaf cell, with a cell wall and chloroplasts. A plant cell!", "d_root": "A root hair cell. No chloroplasts, but look: a cell wall! It's a plant cell.", "trick": "Here's the trick. Some plant cells have no chloroplasts. So check for a cell wall!", "d_fat": "A fat cell. It has a big storage space, but no cell wall. An animal cell!", "d_onion": "An onion cell. A cell wall, but no chloroplasts. A plant cell!", "d_muscle": "A muscle cell. No cell wall, so it's an animal cell!", "clue_q": "So what's the best clue for a plant cell?", "clue_a": "The cell wall! Plant cells have one. Animal cells don't.", "spec_def": "Room seven is the special jobs room. A specialised cell has features that let it do a particular job.", "ruby_hi": "Meet Ruby Root-Hair! She's a root hair cell.", "ruby_job": "Her long, thin arm takes water from the soil. In the book's photo, root hair cells are magnified thirty times.", "ruby_stretch": "Stretch your arm out long, like Ruby!", "ruby_q": "Does Ruby have chloroplasts?", "ruby_a": "No! It's dark underground. No light, so no chloroplasts.", "max_hi": "And this is Max Muscle, a heart muscle cell! In the book's photo, they're magnified five hundred times.", "max_job": "Heart muscle cells work together in heart muscle tissue. They make the heart move.", "max_mito": "Max is packed with mitochondria. Moving needs lots of energy!", "max_squeeze": "Squeeze your fist, like a heart beating!", "feat_intro": "Now match each feature to its job.", "f_mito": "Lots of mitochondria. What's that for?", "f_mito_a": "Lots of energy, to move! Just like Max.", "f_wall": "A thicker cell wall. What's that for?", "f_wall_a": "More support! Cell walls help to support cells.", "f_chl": "Lots of chloroplasts. Where would this cell be?", "f_chl_a": "At the top of a leaf, in the light! Great for photosynthesis.", "f_none": "No chloroplasts at all. Where would this cell be?", "f_none_a": "In a root! No light gets there. Just like Ruby.", "myst_intro": "Four more mystery cells. What job does each one do? Look at its shape.", "m_fat_q": "This animal cell has a huge storage space. What's its job?", "m_fat_a": "Storing things! It's a fat cell.", "m_tube_q": "This plant cell is long, with holes in its end walls. What's its job?", "m_tube_a": "Carrying things! Dissolved sugar flows through the holes, from cell to cell.", "m_musc_q": "This animal cell is packed with mitochondria. What's its job?", "m_musc_a": "Moving! It's a muscle cell, like Max.", "m_root_q": "This plant cell has a long, hair-like part. What's its job?", "m_root_a": "Taking in water! It's a root hair cell, like Ruby.", "spec_done": "Every special cell has a job, and its shape helps it do it!", "room8": "Room eight is the How Big Really room. Time for some gentle maths!", "x600_q": "This cheek cell photo says times six hundred. What does that mean?", "x600_a": "It looks six hundred times bigger than its real size!", "measure": "First, we measure the cell in the photo. Here comes the ruler.", "ruler_q": "How wide is the cell, at its widest part? Read the ruler.", "ruler_wrong": "Look where the cell ends on the ruler. Try again.", "ruler_a": "Twenty-eight millimetres.", "rule": "To find the real size, divide the picture size by the magnification.", "calc_go": "Let's use the calculator. Tap the glowing keys.", "c1_q": "Twenty-eight divided by six hundred. Which answer is right?", "calc_mult": "That's what you get if you multiply. We need to divide.", "calc_add": "That's what you get if you add. We need to divide.", "c1_a": "About zero point zero five millimetres. That's about five hundredths of a millimetre!", "c1_book": "The book says zero point zero four seven. That rounds to zero point zero five.", "tiny": "So tiny! Much smaller than a full stop.", "leaf_intro": "Now the leaf cell photo. It's magnified two hundred and seventy-five times.", "ruler2_q": "How long is this cell? Read the ruler.", "ruler2_a": "Sixty-two millimetres.", "c2_q": "Sixty-two divided by two hundred and seventy-five. Which answer is right?", "c2_a": "About zero point two three millimetres. That's about twenty-three hundredths of a millimetre.", "back_intro": "Now let's check it the other way round. Real size, times magnification, gives the picture size.", "c3_q": "Zero point zero four seven, times six hundred. What do we get?", "c3_a": "About twenty-eight millimetres! The same as the ruler. It works!", "teach_intro": "Oh no, that sneeze muddled my memory! Can you teach me?", "t_q_nucleus": "What does my nucleus do?", "t_q_membrane": "And what does my cell surface membrane do?", "t_explain": "Explain it to me in your own words.", "t_ok_nucleus": "Oh, I remember now! The nucleus controls the cell. Thank you, teacher!", "t_ok_membrane": "Oh yes! It keeps me together, and controls what goes in and out. Thank you!", "t_help_nucleus": "Hmm, let me think. The nucleus controls the cell. Can you say that back to me?", "t_help_membrane": "Hmm, let me think. The membrane controls what goes in and out. Can you say that back to me?", "t_gotit": "Thank you! Now I've got it.", "t_three": "Here are three answers. Tap the right one.", "t_notquite": "Not quite. Try another one.", "t_nohear": "I didn't hear you. Try again, or tap: show me some answers.", "m1": "Plants don't have mitochondria. Only animals do.", "m1_fix": "Of course! Plant cells have mitochondria too. Plants need energy.", "m2": "All plant cells have chloroplasts.", "m2_fix": "Oh yes, root hair cells don't. There's no light underground.", "m3": "The cell wall and the membrane are the same thing.", "m3_fix": "Silly me! The wall is a box outside. The membrane is a thin bag inside.", "teach_wrong": "Hmm, are you sure? Think again.", "teach_done": "You're a brilliant teacher! My memory is back.", "room9": "The last room is the art studio. Let's draw a root hair cell, like Ruby!", "trace": "Trace over the dotted lines with your finger. Take your time.", "traced": "Lovely drawing! Now let's label it.", "nochl": "Remember: no chloroplasts! It's dark underground.", "drawn": "Five labels. A perfect root hair cell!", "paper": "Later, draw it on paper too, with the same five labels.", "f_done": "You did it! I'm a whole cell again!", "answer_bigq": "Plant and animal cells both have a nucleus, cytoplasm, a membrane and mitochondria.", "answer_bigq2": "Plant cells also have a cell wall, a large vacuole, and often chloroplasts.", "f_cert": "Here's your certificate, Cell Detective. Thank you for helping me today!", "f_next": "Next time, we'll explore organ systems. See you there!", "lab_wrong": "Hmm, not quite. Try again.", "n_nucleus": "Nucleus.", "n_cytoplasm": "Cytoplasm.", "n_membrane": "Membrane.", "n_mitochondria": "Mitochondria.", "n_chloroplast": "Chloroplast.", "n_vacuole": "Vacuole.", "n_csm": "Cell surface membrane.", "n_wall": "Cell wall.", "s_nu": "nu.", "s_cle": "cle.", "s_us": "us.", "s_cy": "cy.", "s_to": "to.", "s_plasm": "plasm.", "s_mem": "mem.", "s_brane": "brane.", "s_mi": "mi.", "s_chon": "chon.", "s_dri": "dri.", "s_a": "a.", "s_chlor": "chlor.", "s_o": "o.", "s_plast": "plast.", "s_vac": "vac.", "s_u": "u.", "s_ole": "ole.", "p1": "Brilliant!", "p2": "Yes! You've got it!", "p3": "Spot on, detective!", "p4": "Wonderful!", "p5": "That's it!", "p6": "Amazing work!", "p7": "Yes! Even Cabbage is wobbling with joy!"};
